<title>UK: UK's George sees market disturbance if EMU delayed.</title>
<headline>UK's George sees market disturbance if EMU delayed.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England Governor Eddie George said there could be disturbance on financial markets if a single European currency went ahead without proper convergence or was delayed.</p>
<p>&quot;It's absolutely clear there would be market disturbance, although it is not clear exactly how much,&quot; he said in response to a question after delivering a lecture in London.  </p>
<p>George did not elaborate.</p>
<p>But in the Mais Lecture which he had just delivered, he said there were real risks attached to a single European currency and he was &quot;frankly nervous&quot; at the prospect of launching it at a time of high unemployment.</p>
<p>-- Chizu Nomiyama, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
